{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893971.2, "seq": 13, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.0006504400000000001, "parents": ["Z4"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"], ["score", "progress", "call"]], "n_edges": 2, "editable": ["s1", "s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 596, "out": 1073, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 5.5, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "The change is in `progress`: it clamps the distance gain to 2 so unreachable-tile values (1e9) can't dominate, and it subtracts a penalty for each enemy within 2 tiles of the destination, so the bot prefers safer steps toward the goals. `goal_field` and `score` are unchanged.\n\n```python\n@gene('s4', 'progress toward goals, clamped and penalised near enemies', parents=['s4'])\ndef progress(t: Tile) -> Num:\n    d = at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)\n    danger = count(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, t) <= 2)\n    return min(d, 2) - danger\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: progress line 44: expected Bool, got Num", "birth": 5, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893974.6, "seq": 12, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00057984, "parents": ["Z3"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 370, "out": 977, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 4.6, "stop": "end_turn"}, "genes_changed": ["s4"], "genes_added": [], "genes_removed": [], "added_sizes": [], "lines_changed": 4, "keeps_added": [], "pruned": []}, "error": "behavioural twin", "fingerprint": null, "twin_of": "Z3", "birth": 5, "accepted": false}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893981.1, "seq": 15, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00057684, "parents": ["Z3"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 370, "out": 971, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 5.1, "stop": "end_turn"}, "genes_changed": ["s4"], "genes_added": [], "genes_removed": [], "added_sizes": [], "lines_changed": 3, "keeps_added": [], "pruned": []}, "error": null, "fingerprint": null, "birth": 6, "accepted": true, "name": "Z6", "species": "S1"}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893983.0, "seq": 14, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "cost": 0.0266776, "parents": ["Z4"], "log": {"edges": [["update", "goals", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["Z5a", "s2"], "llm": {"in": 486, "out": 1128, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 15.0, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "```python\nHEALING: Bool = False\n\n@gene('Z5a', 'per-turn cache of the distance field to the goals; tracks a heal-at-home state', parents=['s3'])\ndef update() -> None:\n    hf = me().health_frac\n    if hf < 0.35:\n        HEALING = True\n    elif hf > 0.9:\n        HEALING = False\n    GOAL_FIELD = field(goals(HEALING))\n\n@gene(\"s2\", \"where to walk: home when hurt, an altar with gems, else a cleared group to capture, else a safe living camp group\")\ndef goals(heal: Bool) -> Tiles:\n    if heal:\n        return my_spawn()\n    if gems() > 0:\n        acc = near(tile(-5, -5), 0)\n        for a in altars() - locked_altars():\n            acc = acc | near(a, 0.655)\n        if size(acc) > 0:\n            return acc\n    reward = near(tile(-5, -5), 0)\n    acc = near(tile(-5, -5), 0)\n    for g in range(num_groups()):\n        if group_reward(g):\n            reward = reward | group_tiles(g)\n        elif not group_respawning(g):\n            ts = group_tiles(g)\n            t0 = best(ts, lambda t: 0)\n            k = spawn_type(t0)\n            if k == MONOLITH:\n                continue\n            if k == GOLEM and round() < 600:\n                continue\n            acc = acc | ts\n    if size(reward) > 0:\n        return reward\n    if size(acc) > 0:\n        return acc\n    return my_spawn()\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: goals line 45: unsupported statement Continue", "birth": 6, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893983.9, "seq": 16, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00052964, "parents": ["seed"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"], ["goal_field", "goals", "call"]], "n_edges": 2, "editable": ["s2", "s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 468, "out": 857, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 5.3, "stop": "end_turn"}, "genes_changed": ["s2"], "genes_added": [], "genes_removed": [], "added_sizes": [], "lines_changed": 4, "keeps_added": [], "pruned": []}, "error": null, "fingerprint": null, "birth": 7, "accepted": true, "name": "Z7", "species": "S0"}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893991.9, "seq": 19, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00067074, "parents": ["Z4"], "log": {"edges": [["update", "goal_field", "keep"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["Z5a", "s3"], "llm": {"in": 374, "out": 1158, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 6.5, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation changes `update()` so the distance field routes around monsters. It treats living camp tiles, other than the goal groups themselves, as obstacles, so the bot stops walking through camps and waking them. It also stops the search once the goal tiles are reached, which saves fuel.\n\n```python\n@gene(\"Z5a\", \"per-turn cache of the distance field to the goals, routing around non-goal camps\", parents=[\"s3\"])\ndef update() -> None:\n    g = goals()\n    GOAL_FIELD = field_avoid(g, walls() | (camp_tiles() - g), g)\n```\n\n```python\n@gene(\"s3\", \"distance field to the goals (cached per turn)\", parents=[\"s3\"])\ndef goal_field() -> Field:\n    return GOAL_FIELD\n```"}, "error": "EditError: no change", "birth": 7, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792893993.7, "seq": 18, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00056324, "parents": ["Z4"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"], ["update", "goal_field", "keep"]], "n_edges": 2, "editable": ["Z5a", "s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 434, "out": 931, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 10.7, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "The change makes the cached distance field route around walls, using `field_avoid` with the wall mask and an empty stop set so the whole map is searched. Goals stay reachable at any distance, so `progress` keeps a meaningful gradient. I haven't run this in the arena.\n\n```python\n@gene(\"Z5b\", \"per-turn cache of the wall-avoiding distance field to the goals\", parents=[\"Z5a\"])\ndef update() -> None:\n    GOAL_FIELD = field_avoid(goals(), walls(), walls() - walls())\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: line 50: gene update redefined or shadows a builtin", "birth": 7, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
